#- §6╔═.✵.════════╗
§5      Pest Control!
§6╚════════.✵.═╝
§8Today’s article is all about Endermen! Why? Because they will not leave me or my tavern alone! Ever since my first interview with that strange witch, I’ve been feeling sort of peculiar. Like I’m being watched. I know living in a cave is not  
#- §8the most ideal environment when it comes to hostile mobs. The cave is on top of a huge hill and may as well be on the surface, yet one particular mob still prevails. Always showing up in the magazine office, the tavern itself, my shops and outside. I've had to put a
#- §8warning sign up so any travellers looking for a quick drink don’t get spooked. Having everyone looking down all the time is bad for business! They keep moving parts of my garden, blocking doors with dirt and stealing my moss, which is a step too far! I’ll admit things have calmed down a 
#- §8lot over time. §8As a witch myself, I built a bonfire outside and cast a banishing spell and it seems to have worked for now. Or it might have just smoked them out like people do with wasp nests. The only concern I have is that some people have started acting odd whenever they see me.
#- §8They avoid me now as if I’m an Enderman myself. I’ll be working at my desk, §oignoring the noises, §0§8and someone will drop in to purchase the magazine and just, stand there, looking at me. Or rather not looking at me. Maybe the spell backfired. 
I have seen purple floating specs of light
#- §8in the §8corner of my eyes, and feel like I randomly grow about a block and a half in height at random moments. 

Ah well, the good news is the Endermen pest control is working…I think! Maybe I should start selling carved pumpkins? For health and safety reasons…
#- -------------------
If you have seen me looking ‘§onot myself§0’ lately, please feel free to let me know by emailing me at:
§8
§nmailmag@lookdown.com§0
-------------------

§6        (｢⊙_☉)｢ ʷʱʸ?

