#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗  §2  ᴘʀᴏʟᴏɢᴜᴇ ᴘᴀʀᴛ ᴛᴡᴏ
§5╚════════.✵.═╝
§2Day slowly turned into night as a deep purple blanket of glittering stars shined above. The villagers gathered around the small plant waiting for the miracle they’d been promised. As the full moon reached it’s peak and all was
#- §2covered in silver light, the leaves of the plant started to glow a soft golden hue. A comforting warmth could be felt as the golden light turned into seeds. Like raindrops hanging from each stem. The villagers did as instructed and gathered up the seeds of light and
#- §2scattered them into the wind. They followed them as each one, as if they had a will of their own, floated gracefully around and rested on the ground.
Some took them to fresh water sources. Some took them to lush grassland filled with the most beautiful flowers. Some took 
#- §2them to caves filled with far more than gold, even emeralds and diamonds. Some revealed crumbling temples and sunken ships from civilisations long gone with loot inside and shelter. More importantly, the last remaining seeds of light guided them to giant forests of all kinds. Enough wood to
#- §2last a lifetime. §2The witches' spell had worked. Overjoyed, the villagers returned to the fern and the witch waiting for them. They showered her with thanks and praise. The tiny plant was still as it was, except for one twinkle of light. “§6I still have mine left§2,” the witch said as she carefully 
#- §2plucked the last seed and held it tightly in her palm. The witch threw it high into the air and spoke softly; “§6my hidden gold is the one treasure I could never have… a child of my own§2”. The light slowly fell back down and engulfed the small fern. Blinded by the light the villagers turned their heads 
#- §2for just a few seconds. When they turned back their eyes met with the bewitching green eyes of a young girl. Her hair was brown like dark oak and her skin was a pale shade of moss. Her clothes were formed with the textures of leaves and flower petals... 
#- §2A bee landed on her head as the crowd of shocked faces stood all around her. 

“§6My name is Fern, and it’s bad manners to keep a plant from growing§2."
          
